6. Design Rationale

The system design was guided by architectural principles from the course:

 Key Decisions
Use of architectural styles to structure the system
Use of components and connectors as core building blocks
Adoption of compound components for modular organisation
 Why These Choices?
Layered architecture → clear separation of concerns
MVC → separation of UI, logic, and control
SOA principles → independent, loosely coupled services

These decisions align with the idea that architectural styles provide:

Reusable design patterns
Well-defined interaction semantics
Scalable system structures
